  "question": {
    "text": "A person in a lift is holding a water jar, which has a small hole at the lower end of its side. When the lift is at rest, the water jet coming out of the hole hits the floor of the lift at a distance d of 1.2 m from the person. In the following, state of the lift&#39;s motion is given in List I and the distance where the water jet hits the floor of the lift is given in List II. Match the statements from List I with those in List II and select the correct answer using the code given below the lists.<br />&nbsp;<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List I</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List II</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A.</td>\t\t\t<td>Lift is accelerating vertically up.</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mo>P.</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B.</td>\t\t\t<td>Lift is accelerating vertically down with an acceleration less than the gravitational acceleration.</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mo>Q.</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C.</td>\t\t\t<td>Lift is moving vertically up with constant speed.</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mo>R.</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D.</td>\t\t\t<td>Lift is falling freely.</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mo>S.</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>No water leaks out of the jar</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>",
    "image": null
  },
