  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In P, Q, R no horizontal velocity is imparted to falling water, so d remains same.<br />In S, since its free fall, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> liquid won't fall with respect to lift.",
